<title>HONG KONG: Auckland/Melbourne air cargo up 39.8pct in Feb/Jan.</title>
<headline>Auckland/Melbourne air cargo up 39.8pct in Feb/Jan.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>There was a 39.8 percent increase in the amount of airfreight on inbound and outbound flights between Auckland and Melbourne in the year to end January 1997 compared to Feb-Jan 1995/96, statistics issued by Australia's Department of Transport and Regional Development show.</p>
<p>Auckland-Sydney remained the major route accounting for 7.2 pct of overall freight percent of the total air freight for the year to end-January, said the department.</p>
<p>There was a significant fall in the amount of airfreight carried between Hong Kong and Melbourne, which recorded a 16.7 percent drop. Los Angeles-Sydney recorded an 11.5 per cent fall.</p>
<p>Detail in tonnnes for the years to end-Jan '97 and end-Jan '96 for the top 10 international city pairs, with percentage changes include:</p>
<p>City Pair	     1996/97*  1995/96   Pct move</p>
<p>Sydney with</p>
<p>  Auckland	     42,749    40,536     up  5.5</p>
<p>  Singapore	    36,534    34,005     up  7.4</p>
<p>  Hong Kong	    35,638    34,994     up  1.8</p>
<p>  Los Angeles	  27,959    31,575   down 11.5</p>
<p>  Tokyo		  21,515    22,062   down  2.5</p>
<p>  Oska		   12,642    11,940     up  5.9</p>
<p>Melbourne with</p>
<p>  Hong Kong	    22,654    27,191   down 16.7</p>
<p>  Auckland	     33,930    24,273     up 39.8</p>
<p>  Singapore	    29,609    30,036   down  1.4</p>
<p>Perth with</p>
<p>  Singapore	    20,805    18,986     up  9.6</p>
<p> Other Australian   307,313   277,335     up 10.8</p>
<p> All Australian     591,348   552,933     up  6.9</p>
<p>* Jan '97 figures provisional</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
